WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.919
Chris Pratt went from that funny chubby guy
on Parks and Recreation to bonafide movie

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:07.620
star almost overnight thanks to his starring
roles in blockbusters like Guardians of the

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.330
Galaxy and and Jurassic World.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.250
But for much of his early career, it seemed
as if he was destined to play on the sidelines,

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.310
as boyfriends in romantic comedies or co-workers
with only a handful of lines.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.960
Here are some under-the-radar roles Pratt
played before he became a global superstar.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.270
Everwood

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:27.289
Pratt's first big break came in 2002 when
he was cast as Bright Abbott, a jock with

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:30.890
a heart of gold, on the critically acclaimed
WB series Everwood.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:34.039
Pratt stayed with the show throughout its
four-season run, most of which dealt with

00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:36.629
Bright's on-again, off-again relationship
with Hannah.

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:40.739
In real life, though, Pratt wound up dating
his on-screen sister, Revenge's Emily Van

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.059
Camp, for a number of years.

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:44.399
They split in 2007.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:45.500
Strangers With Candy

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:51.430
In 2005, Pratt landed a part in the big-screen
version of Amy Sedaris' cult TV comedy, Strangers

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.430
with Candy.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:56.339
In it, he played Brason, another high school
jock who becomes the object of Jerri Blank's

00:00:56.339 --> 00:00:58.019
lusty, wacked-out desires.

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:02.079
As far as the Chris Pratt Film Canon goes,
Strangers with Candy will likely be remembered

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:06.070
best as That Time Chris Rocked a Hilarious,
If Unfortunate, Mullet.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:07.070
The O.C.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.259
By the time The O.C. headed into its fourth
and final season, most people had abandoned

00:01:11.259 --> 00:01:15.450
the once top-rated teen soap due to its recycled
plotlines and stale acting.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:19.640
Those who stuck around, however, were treated
to an unexpected creative revival, due in

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.289
great part to Pratt's performance as Summer's
free-spirited dorm-mate, Che.

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:26.930
Pratt infused the show with laughs, heart,
and welcomed weirdness, allowing The O.C.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:29.969
to end on a higher note than anyone could
have hoped.

00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:30.969
Wanted

00:01:30.969 --> 00:01:34.540
Although Pratt is now known for playing hunky,
charming leading men, there was a time in

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.210
his career when he was relegated to roles
like "That Coworker You Just Want to Punch

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.210
in the Face."

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.750
Such was the case in the 2008 Angelina Jolie
action flick Wanted, in which Pratt angered

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.040
co-star James McAvoy's character so much,
he eventually got smacked in the face with

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.229
a keyboard.

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:51.391
"Yeah, that was great, bro.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:51.900
Who's the man?"

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.200
Bride Wars

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.750
Another pre-fame role Pratt had to try on
for size: playing the bro-y, suit-and-tie-wearing

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:03.939
fiance, as seen in the disastrous 2009 rom-com
Bride Wars.

00:02:03.939 --> 00:02:07.659
Fortunately for Pratt fans, his role in the
embarrassing flop was overshadowed by the

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:12.750
insane antics of Kate Hudson and Pratt's on-screen
love interest, Anne Hathaway.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:13.750
Moneyball

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:18.010
Pratt got his first legitimate taste of prestige,
award-winning movies when Sony cast him to

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:22.670
play real-life first baseman, Scott Hatteberg,
in the 2011 baseball drama Moneyball.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.990
"What's your biggest fear?"

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:29.360
"A baseball being hit in my general direction."

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.270
Although the role was small, Pratt held his
own opposite his mega-famous co-star, Brad

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.190
Pitt, and even dropped 30 pounds to secure
the role.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:40.920
Moneyball marked a stark contrast to Pratt's
goofy, affable Andy on Parks and Recreation,

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.700
setting him up for big movie roles for years
to come.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.330
Zero Dark Thirty

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.910
One year after Moneyball hit theaters, Pratt
once again found himself at the center of

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:53.480
an awards-magnet movie — this time, in Kathryn
Bigelow's Zero Dark Thirty, about the U.S.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.310
hunt for Osama bin Laden.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:58.420
Pratt played one of the Navy SEALs who helped
take bin Laden down.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.860
"So UBL?

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.280
You got an intel source on the ground?"

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.280
"No."

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.280
"No?

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.500
Okay, so how do you know it's Bin Laden?"

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.840
Her

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.000
In 2013, Pratt appeared in his third-consecutive
Best Picture nominee, Her, from writer-director

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.180
Spike Jonze.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.681
This time around, he played a coworker who
goes out on a double-date with Joaquin

00:03:18.681 --> 00:03:23.310
Phoenix and his virtual, body-less girlfriend
Samantha, voiced by Scarlett Johansson — which

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.950
is just as weird as it sounds.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.281
"I didn't mean it like that.

00:03:26.281 --> 00:03:27.660
I just meant that it was a different experience."

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.270
"No, no, no, Samantha, we know exactly what
you mean.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.020
We're all dumb humans."

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.040
Thanks for watching!

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.540
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.680
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

